      "answer": "Ambessa is a fighter and assassin who combines physical ability damage with empowered attacks that restore energy. Her ability-linked dashes let her reposition, but cannot cross terrain or occur while immobilized or grounded. Her ultimate blinks her to the farthest enemy champion in a chosen line.",
      "build_focus": "AD",
      "card_id": "champ:ambessa:overview:L1",
      "counterplay": "Limit her access to attacks and use grounding or immobilization to restrict her dashes.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Name: Ambessa. Official role tags: Fighter, Assassin.",
              "source_id": "riot:role"
            },
            {
              "quote": "Active: Ambessa slashes with her twin drakehounds in the target direction, dealing physical damage to enemies hit.",
              "source_id": "wiki:cunningsweep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "Medarda Maxim: Ambessa's next basic attack gains range, bonus attack speed, deals bonus physical damage, and restores energy.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Ambessa is a fighter and assassin who combines physical ability damage with empowered attacks that restore energy."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Entering an attack or movement command while casting an ability will cause Ambessa to dash a short distance once the ability is cast",
              "source_id": "riot:P"
            },
            {
              "quote": "This dash cannot pass through terrain.Ambessa cannot dash while immobilized or grounded.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Her ability-linked dashes let her reposition, but cannot cross terrain or occur while immobilized or grounded."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Ambessa blinks to the farthest enemy champion in a line of her choosing and suppresses them upon her arrival.",
              "source_id": "riot:R"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Her ultimate blinks her to the farthest enemy champion in a chosen line."
        }
      ],
      "priority": "A",
      "priority_reason": "Her attack cycle and mobility limits shape engagements.",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "answer": "During the brief period of an ability cast when Ambessa cannot act, an attack or movement command can queue a dash toward that target or location afterward; later commands can replace or cancel it, and she cannot dash through terrain or while immobilized or grounded. Ability casts grant temporary Medarda Maxim stacks, up to three, refreshed by further casts; basic attacks consume one each for extra range, attack speed, physical damage, and energy restoration. Ambessa sees an indicator of her dash direction and destination, while her empowered-attack pips are visible only to her player.",
      "build_focus": "",
      "card_id": "champ:ambessa:system:p:drakehoundsstep:recognize:L2",
      "counterplay": "Deny attack access to limit energy restoration, and use grounding or immobilization to restrict repositioning.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "During the lockout of Ambessa's abilities, inputting an attack or movement command causes her to dash to or towards the target or location, respectively, after the lockout ends.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "Active: Ambessa braces herself for up to 0.5 seconds, during which in the first 0.225 seconds she is unable to act.",
              "source_id": "wiki:repudiation"
            },
            {
              "quote": "If multiple attack and movement commands are inputted during the lockout of an ability, the most recent one is used for the dash's targeting.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "If the most recent input is not an attack or movement command, the dash will not trigger.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "This dash cannot pass through terrain.Ambessa cannot dash while immobilized or grounded.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "During the brief period of an ability cast when Ambessa cannot act, an attack or movement command can queue a dash toward that target or location afterward; later commands can replace or cancel it, and she cannot dash through terrain or while immobilized or grounded."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Whenever Ambessa casts an ability, she generates a stack of Medarda Maxim after the ability's respective lockout for 4 seconds, refreshing with subsequent casts and stacking up to 3 times. Basic attacks consume one stack each to become empowered.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "Medarda Maxim: Ambessa's next basic attack gains range, bonus attack speed, deals bonus physical damage, and restores energy.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Ability casts grant temporary Medarda Maxim stacks, up to three, refreshed by further casts; basic attacks consume one each for extra range, attack speed, physical damage, and energy restoration."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "During Drakehound's Step, a visual indicator is visible to Ambessa displaying the eventual dash's direction and destination location.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "The number of available attacks empowered by Medarda Maxim are visible as pips under Ambessa's health bar, only visible to the player.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Ambessa sees an indicator of her dash direction and destination, while her empowered-attack pips are visible only to her player."
        }
      ],
      "priority": "A",
      "priority_reason": "Explains her repeated repositioning and energy recovery.",
      "uncertainties": [
        "The frozen indicator core calls both indicators private, but the evidence expressly establishes exclusivity only for attack pips. The answer retains both indicators without asserting dash-indicator exclusivity.",
        "Immobilization or grounding during the ability lockout can cancel the buffered dash even if the control ends before she could dash."
      ]
    },
    {
